6919       * Compute P(Yj|Xi) values from conjectured betas;
6920       data Exemplary;
6921       _B0 = 0;
6922       _B1 = -1.5;
6923       _B2 = 0.5;
6924       _B3 = 2;
6925       do X1 = 0 to 1;
6926       do X2 = 0 to 1;
6927       _pi = logistic(_B0 + _B1*X1 + _B2*X2 + _B3*X1*X2);
6928       do Y = 0 to 1;
6929       PY = _pi**Y * (1-_pi)**(1-Y);
6930       output;
6931       end;
6932       end;
6933       end;
6934       keep X1 X2 Y PY;
6935       run;

NOTE: The data set WORK.EXEMPLARY has 8 observations and 4 variables.

6936       proc print data=Exemplary;
6937       run;

NOTE: There were 8 observations read from the data set WORK.EXEMPLARY.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE PRINT printed page 548.

6938       * Expand according to relative allocations of design profiles;
6939       data Exemplary;
6940       set Exemplary;
6941       if (X1 = 0 and X2 = 0) then _alloc=4;
6942       else if (X1 = 0 and X2 = 1) then _alloc=5;
6943       else if (X1 = 1 and X2 = 0) then _alloc=5;
6944       else _alloc=6;
6945       do _i = 1 to _alloc;
6946       output;
6947       end;
6948       keep X1 X2 Y PY;
6949       run;

NOTE: There were 8 observations read from the data set WORK.EXEMPLARY.
NOTE: The data set WORK.EXEMPLARY has 40 observations and 4 variables.

