6964       * Fetch -2LogL for full model;
6965       data statsFull;
6966       set statsFull;
6967       where Criterion = "-2 Log L";
6968       Neg2LogLFull = InterceptAndCovariates;
6969       keep Neg2LogLFull;
6970       run;

NOTE: There were 1 observations read from the data set WORK.STATSFULL.
      WHERE Criterion='-2 Log L';
NOTE: The data set WORK.STATSFULL has 1 observations and 1 variables.

6971       * Run reduced model;
6972       proc logistic data=Exemplary;
6973       ods output fitstatistics=statsRed;
6974       weight PY;
6975       model Y = X1 X2;
6976       run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is modeling the probability that Y=0. One way to change this to model the probability that Y=1 is to specify the response variable option 
